cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  The Performance Measurement System for B2B Software Companies
  in the AI-Era
message: >-
  If you reference or build on this design, please cite it using
  the metadata below.
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  A performance measurement system designed from first principles.
  It surveys the systems used at Google, Amazon, Netflix, Apple,
  Meta, Microsoft and Deloitte/Adobe with an explicit adopt/reject
  decision for each, then specifies a four-layer architecture that
  decouples development signal from compensation decisions. The
  design responds to two findings convention ignores: that the four
  purposes of a performance system have contradictory information
  requirements, and that the majority of variance in a performance
  rating is attributable to the rater rather than the person rated.
